invariant: INV-16
file: hkdf.h
catches: hash_runtime_test
reason: hkdf_extract_cpu calls the copy on the instructions for a value that
  does not name them, and hkdf.c for one that does. The early secret, the
  handshake secret and a QUIC Initial secret of a session without
  CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA256 then run SHA-256 instructions over the PSK
  and the key exchange's output (docs/decisions.md 93). The bytes are the
  same. bin/hash_runtime_test counts the calls each entry makes into each
  path under every ch_cfg.cpu value.

--- old
    if (hash_on_instructions(cpu, hash_len)) {
        hkdf_extract_hw(hash_len, salt, salt_len, ikm, ikm_len, prk);
--- new
    if (!hash_on_instructions(cpu, hash_len)) {
        hkdf_extract_hw(hash_len, salt, salt_len, ikm, ikm_len, prk);
